  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Peter de Savary was a British entrepreneur, hotelier and yachtsman whose ventures ranged from international clubs and resorts to property, shipyards and marinas. He developed St James’s Clubs, Skibo and Bovey castles, and landmarks including Land’s End. In sport, he led Britain’s 1983 America’s Cup challenge and founded the shipbuilder Pendennis Shipyard.",
